        "Content": "FOR SALE BY PRIVATE TREATY\r\nBEAUTIFULLY PRESENTED 4 BEDROOM EXTENDED BUNGALOW ON LARGE LANDSCAPED SITE IN HIGHLY CONVENIENT LOCATION 3 MILES ATHENRY TOWN AND 2.5 MILES MONIVEA VILLAGE\r\n\r\n \r\nKNOCKBRACK, ATHENRY, \r\nCO. GALWAY\r\nH65 VY04\r\n\r\nLOCATION:  \r\n\r\nThe property is located at Knockbrack, Athenry, Co. Galway and is situated approximately 3 miles from the Medieval and Heritage town of Athenry and 2.5 miles from Monivea Village on the main Athenry / Monivea Road.\r\n\r\nAll local residential amenities and facilities are available in the nearby town of Athenry and the picturesque village of Monivea.  Galway City is within approximately 17 miles from the property.  Newcastle NS is just under 1.5 miles with it’s fine National School , church and playing pitch. \r\n\r\nAthenry is a highly sought after commuter town of Galway City which is just 13 miles and is steeped in local history and is a famous Medieval, Heritage and Market town. Athenry has  excellent road and rail services and avails of Motorway access from the M6 Galway-Dublin route and with easy access on to the M17/M18 route further out from the town. Athenry train station boasts an excellent service to Galway/ Dublin and Athlone etc aswell as the Galway / Limerick route .\r\n \r\nDESCRIPTION:\r\n\r\nThe property comprises a beautifully presented spacious 4 bedroom extended bungalow residence of approximately 1,520 sq ft and stands on a highly attractive large lawned site with some outbuildings.  The property has a front tarmac driveway  which wraps around to the rear offering a spacious forecourt with a stylish raised deck area being a lovely feature looking down over the expansive rear garden with picturesque country views.  \r\n\r\nThe house benefits from a major renovation and upgrade works in recent years including the addition of a lovely rear family room extension annexe off the kitchen / dining room with patio doors leading out to the feature raised decking area allowing for modern family living.  The upgrade works include quality new windows and doors throughout, dual central heating, with a feature new stove to family room ,  new bathroom suites, new kitchen with feature granite worktop, flooring and the lovely rear raised deck capturing the evening sun and overlooking the rear garden.  The property also benefits from pumped insulation to cavity walls and attic insulation.  \r\n\r\nThe house is beautifully finished and is in ready to walk into condition and equally the gardens and outside are truly impressive providing for a superb family home in a highly convenient location.  \r\n\r\n\r\nExtra Features:\r\n•\tFloored attic with STIRA \r\n•\tInsulated walls and attic\r\n•\tPVC fascia and soffit \r\n•\tPVC double glazed windows – Recently installed \r\n•\tSolid fuel stove to family room with back boiler \r\n•\tBuilt in storage seat units \r\n•\tLaminate walnut floor \r\n•\tDouble patio doors \r\n•\tCoving and recessed lights \r\n•\tExpansive views to back garden and countryside \r\n•\tOil fired central heating – solid fuel – dual central heating \r\n•\tNew pump to outdoor boiler\r\n•\tFitted alarm \r\n\r\nBER Cert:\t111602686\r\nBER: C1\t \t\r\n\r\nSERVICES:  Septic tank, Mains water. We have not tested any services.\r\n\r\nGUIDE PRICE:\r\n€485,000\r\n\r\nSIGNS:\r\nOur for sale sign is on display at the property \r\n\r\nVIEWINGS:\r\nViewings are strictly by appointment with CATHAL MORAN AUCTIONEERS who are Sole Selling Agents"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
